      "text": "**Singapore’s air quality is unhealthy right now.** As of about **4:15 a.m. Singapore time on October 17**, the latest official readings show 24-hour PSI ranging from **146 in the North to 196 in Central**. One-hour PM2.5 is **60–108 µg/m³ across regions**, which NEA classifies as **Elevated**. ([api-open.data.gov.sg](https://api-open.data.gov.sg/v2/real-time/api/psi))\n\nNEA advises reducing strenuous outdoor activity when PM2.5 is Elevated. The 24-hour PSI is a guide for planning; check the one-hour PM2.5 for immediate decisions. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026))",
